Description: declare lilv.py as intentionally not installed
 lilv's waf build system installs a ctypes-based Python wrapper at
 .
   debian/tmp/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lilv.py
 .
 when `python3:native` is present in the build environment (which
 it always is in our build container).  The wrapper is ~one file —
 a thin ctypes binding that dlopens `liblilv-0.so.0` at runtime.
 .
 None of lilv's three declared binary packages — `liblilv-0-0`,
 `liblilv-dev`, `lilv-utils` — claims this file in its `.install`
 list.  Under `debhelper-compat (= 13)`'s default-strict
 `dh_missing`, an unshipped file in `debian/tmp/` is a build error:
 .
   dh_missing: warning: usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lilv.py exists in debian/tmp but is not installed to anywhere
   dh_missing: error: missing files, aborting
 .
 dh_missing's own recommendation when the omission is intentional:
 .
   "If the omission is intentional or no other helper can take care
    of this consider adding the paths to debian/not-installed."
 .
 Add a `debian/not-installed` declaring the Python wrapper as
 intentionally not shipped.  The ctypes wrapper has no consumer
 in our build (no `python3-lilv` package is declared upstream;
 introducing one here would be a much larger packaging change),
 so dropping it on the floor is the right call.
 .
 If a future Athena variant wants the Python binding, the right
 path is to add a new `python3-lilv` binary package to
 `debian/control` + a matching `python3-lilv.install` claiming
 the file — NOT to revert this patch.
 .
 Surfaced during GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-15 — lilv
 is pulled in by the LV2 audio plugin host stack (likely transitive
 via gnome-shell → tracker → libnice or similar audio handling).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-15
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/not-installed
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# The waf build installs a ctypes Python wrapper at this path when
+# python3:native is available.  Lilv ships no python3-lilv binary
+# package, so the file is intentionally unshipped.  See the
+# 9001-declare-python-binding-not-installed.patch DEP-3 header.
+usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/lilv.py
